==German==
{{wikipedia|dab=Hahn|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|hano}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*hanô}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*kan-|t=to sing}}. Compare {{cog|nl|haan}}, {{cog|da|hane}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hɑːn/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Hahn.OGG|audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aːn|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Hahns|gen2=Hahnes|Hähne|pl2=Hahnen|Hähnchen|dim2=Hähnlein}}

# [[cock]], [[rooster]]
# [[stopcock]], [[tap]], [[spigot]], [[faucet]]

====Usage notes====
* The normal plural is '''''Hähne'''''.
* The plural ''Hahnen'' is obsolete or dialectal (the last remnant of what was once a weak noun).

